{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Custom State and Traits","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TraitKey"],"anchor":"Custom-State-and-Traits"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine only ever branches on a closed set of traits and scalar globals, and that is what keeps its behavior auditable: every decision it can make is visible in a handful of small enums. Your game’s own data does not have to live in that set. A wallet, a set of combat stats, an item’s price — custom state and custom traits ride along type-erased through the same storage the engine already saves and restores, read by your rules and by nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Rich `@Global` state","anchor":"Rich-Global-state","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type can be a global. Conform it to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue"},{"text":" with an empty conformance — the default implementation JSON-boxes it into the type-erased ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" case, so there’s nothing to hand-pack:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Purse: Codable, Sendable, GlobalValue {","    var coins: Int","    var receipts: [String] = []","}","","struct MyGame: Game {","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)","    \/\/ …","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read and write it in rules exactly like a scalar global — it participates in the turn’s commit and in save\/restore through the one world-state funnel:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["lantern.before(.buy) {","    guard purse.coins >= 5 else { try refuse(\"You can't afford it.\") }","    purse.coins -= 5","    try reply(\"Sold. You have \\(purse.coins) coins left.\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The type needs only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The boxed bytes are what participate in the world state’s equality and hashing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Those bytes are the reason to touch a struct global once per rule body rather than field by field. Reading one decodes and writing one encodes, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"purse.coins -= 5","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a decode, a mutate and an encode — fine on its own, but a rule that sets four fields pays for four round trips and, worse, loses an update if a nested expression writes the same global between the read and the write. Read it into a local, mutate the local, and assign it back once:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var wallet = purse","wallet.coins -= 5","wallet.receipts.append(\"lantern\")","purse = wallet"]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom global is stored as opaque bytes, so if you change its shape, an old save may no longer decode — and a stored value that fails to decode is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not a fall back to the declared default. (The default is only reached when the global’s ID is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" from the save, which is what happens when you add a whole new global.) Save validation cannot catch it first: it checks only that a ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" case is still a ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" case, and one payload looks like another. So keep custom state structs additive and optional-tolerant — new fields with defaults, and a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that keeps the default when a field won’t decode. Versioned codecs are a later effort.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","text":"Custom traits","anchor":"Custom-traits","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a typed key once, then use it to declare a custom property inside an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Item { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Location { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trait(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The value is boxed with the same rule as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a scalar or a whole struct both work:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }","extension TraitKey<String> { static let region = Self(\"region\") }","","let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    trait(.price, 5)","}","","let docks = Location {","    name(\"The Docks\")","    trait(.region, \"waterfront\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read it back on the live proxy with the typed subscript, which returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the trait is absent or stored as a different type:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let price = lantern[.price] ?? 0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A key declared with a default ("},{"code":"TraitKey(\"weight\", default: 1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") can be read as a non-optional "},{"code":"V","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"code":"item[default: .weight]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom traits are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"immutable declared facts"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — they never touch the world state. For per-entity state that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"changes"}]},{"type":"text","text":" during play (an item’s current charge, a creature’s HP), use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":" keyed however your system needs; traits are for the fixed properties an entity is born with."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Worked example","anchor":"Worked-example","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lighthouse"}]},{"type":"text","text":" example ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/"},{"type":"text","text":") keeps two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":"s — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tideStage"},{"type":"text","text":", bumped by a daemon and read by a room’s live description, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keeperGreeted"},{"type":"text","text":", flipped by a dialogue rule — a compact look at custom state driving prose and branching."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/CustomStateGames.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShopGame"},{"type":"text","text":": a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purse"},{"type":"text","text":" struct held in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":", a lantern with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trait(.price, 5)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a game-defined "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"buy"},{"type":"text","text":" verb whose rule reads the price and debits the purse — the commerce plugin in miniature. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStateTests"},{"type":"text","text":" boots it and confirms the struct global round-trips through save\/restore, the custom trait reads back through the typed subscript, and absent\/wrong-type reads return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"See also","level":2,"anchor":"See-also"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"role":"article","title":"Custom State and Traits"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core."}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GlobalValue":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlobalValue"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlobalValue"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Types usable with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property wrapper.","type":"text"}],"title":"GlobalValue","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/globalvalue","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/StateValue":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateValue"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateValue"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/statevalue","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value that can live in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldState"},{"type":"text","text":"’s global storage. The scalar cases"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each pair with a dedicated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GlobalValue"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the type-erased case that carries any other "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" value, so custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state structs and custom traits need no new case of their own."}],"title":"StateValue","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Plugins":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Package a reusable game system as an importable unit of verbs and rules.","type":"text"}],"title":"Plugins","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","abstract":[{"text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world.","type":"text"}],"title":"Writing Rules","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TraitKey":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TraitKey"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TraitKey","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/traitkey","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A typed handle for a custom trait, replacing the stringly-typed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"trait(\"price\", 5)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"item.trait(\"price\", as: Int.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single declaration that carries its own value type:","type":"text"}],"title":"TraitKey","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TraitKey","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Global":{"type":"topic","title":"Global","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom game state with the same ergonomics as built-in state:"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Global"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/global","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Global"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/StateValue/data(typeName:bytes:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"data","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"typeName","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bytes","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Data","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4DataV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/statevalue\/data(typename:bytes:)","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"StateValue.data(typeName:bytes:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto"}}}